    "html": "<p>Each page shows a screenshot with red numbers, and what the button with that number does. Turn pages with <b>← →</b>, and click a picture to enlarge it.</p>\n<h3 data-sec=\"0\">Title Screen</h3>\n<div class=\"gb-duo\"><figure class=\"gb-fig\"><img data-gk=\"guide/p01_title\" alt=\"Title screen\"><figcaption>Title screen</figcaption></figure><table class=\"gb-table gb-legend\"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Button</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span>1</span></td><td>New Voyage</td><td>Create your admiral and start in your home port on May 1, 1480</td></tr><tr><td><span>2</span></td><td>First Voyage (Tutorial)</td><td>An 18-step guided voyage starting in Seville in 1480. Your crew teach you one thing at a time</td></tr><tr><td><span>3</span></td><td>Story: Father's Photo</td><td>Story mode that follows a set plot</td></tr><tr><td><span>4</span></td><td>Load Logbook</td><td>Load from 5 autosave slots and 5 inn logbook slots</td></tr><tr><td><span>5</span></td><td>Controls</td><td>A summary of key controls, and this guidebook</td></tr><tr><td><span>6</span></td><td>Display · Fonts</td><td>Text size, font and text rendering (two pages on)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3 data-sec=\"1\">Creating Your Admiral</h3>\n<div class=\"gb-duo\"><figure class=\"gb-fig\"><img data-gk=\"guide/p02_create\" alt=\"Creating your admiral\"><figcaption>Creating your admiral</figcaption></figure><table class=\"gb-table gb-legend\"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Button</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span>1</span></td><td>Previous face · Next face</td><td>Choose your looks. At forty your admiral turns into a bearded man in his forties</td></tr><tr><td><span>2</span></td><td>Given name · Surname</td><td>Entered separately. The button beside each gives another name</td></tr><tr><td><span>3</span></td><td>Birthday</td><td>Sets your star sign, which gives +6 to one stat</td></tr><tr><td><span>4</span></td><td>Age (18–40)</td><td>Younger means more Vitality and Strength; older means more Intelligence and Charm, and more bonus points</td></tr><tr><td><span>5</span></td><td>Nationality</td><td>Portugal (start in Lisbon) · Spain (start in Seville)</td></tr><tr><td><span>6</span></td><td>Profession</td><td>Each starts with different skills (table below)</td></tr><tr><td><span>7</span></td><td>Difficulty</td><td>Easy · Normal · Strict Rules (table below)</td></tr><tr><td><span>8</span></td><td>Stats ＋ −</td><td>Spread your age bonus points over Vitality, Intelligence, Strength and Charm</td></tr><tr><td><span>9</span></td><td>Reroll</td><td>Roll new stats</td></tr><tr><td><span>10</span></td><td>Skills · Languages ＋ −</td><td>Spend remaining points on skills (17 kinds) and languages</td></tr><tr><td><span>11</span></td><td>Back to Title</td><td>Stop creating</td></tr><tr><td><span>12</span></td><td>Ready to Sail</td><td>Start the game as is</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3 data-sec=\"2\">Professions and Difficulty</h3>\n<ul><li>Age bonus: stat points 4 + (age − 18) × 0.5, skill points 3 + (age − 18) ÷ 4.</li><li>Learning bonus: from Intelligence 40, +1 skill point for every 15 (up to +3); +4 at Intelligence 99 or above.</li></ul>\n<table class=\"gb-table\"><thead><tr><th>Profession</th><th>Starting skills</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Explorer</td><td>Navigation 2 · Surveying 2 · Seamanship 1</td></tr><tr><td>Excavator</td><td>History 2 · Eloquence 2</td></tr><tr><td>Hunter</td><td>Seamanship 3 · Science 1</td></tr><tr><td>Conquistador</td><td>Swordplay 3 · Gunnery 1</td></tr><tr><td>Missionary</td><td>Theology 3 · Eloquence 1</td></tr><tr><td>Merchant</td><td>Accounting 3 · Eloquence 1 (first ship: a Caravel)</td></tr><tr><td>Soldier</td><td>Gunnery 2 · Marksmanship 2</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table class=\"gb-table\"><thead><tr><th>Difficulty</th><th>Entering/leaving port</th><th>Starting money</th><th>Saving</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Easy</td><td>1 day</td><td>5,000 gold</td><td>Anywhere</td></tr><tr><td>Normal</td><td>3 days</td><td>3,000 gold</td><td>At inns</td></tr><tr><td>Strict Rules</td><td>10 days</td><td>3,000 gold</td><td>Only at inns in your home country's cities</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3 data-sec=\"3\">Display · Fonts</h3>\n<div class=\"gb-duo\"><figure class=\"gb-fig\"><img data-gk=\"guide/p03_display\" alt=\"Display · Fonts window\"><figcaption>Display · Fonts window</figcaption></figure><table class=\"gb-table gb-legend\"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Button</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span>1</span></td><td>Text size</td><td>DEFAULT is set to suit your monitor's size and pixel density. Windows and menus grow and shrink with it (remembered on this device only)</td></tr><tr><td><span>2</span></td><td>Font</td><td>DEFAULT is Nanum Myeongjo on dense screens, Noto Serif on coarser ones</td></tr><tr><td><span>3</span></td><td>Text rendering</td><td>Sharp (default): redraws text at the monitor's real size · Classic: stretches the whole screen</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3 data-sec=\"4\">Saving</h3>\n<ul><li><b>Autosave</b> — while you play, the game saves every minute, rotating through 5 slots (overwriting the oldest first). You can turn it off in Settings.</li><li><b>Inn logbook</b> — at an inn, use \"Services → Write in the Logbook (Save)\", or save at your home; pick one of 5 slots.</li><li>On \"Strict Rules\" difficulty you can only write your logbook at inns in your home country's cities.</li></ul>"
